<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Red Flag, 2017</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Red&amp;nbsp;Flag 2017&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt; July 19 2017 / 04:00:00 Zulu &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;Nevada, USA&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; Blue &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Designer: &lt;/B&gt;Tomcat84 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Introduction&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;Red Flag is a world famous exercise held multiple times per year at Nellis AFB, Nevada. It is the "mother of all Flags" and features everything a fighter pilot can wish for in an exercise: dedicated adversary fighters, lots of SAM transmitters, good airspace, and plenty of&amp;nbsp;live bombing targets. It focuses primarily on fighter aircraft working together in COMAO packages to accomplish challenging objectives.&amp;nbsp;Two missions (one day, one night)&amp;nbsp;are flown each day for two weeks, with various assignments, such as Defensive Counter Air, Air Interdiction, Escort, Dynamic Targeting, combinations of the above and more.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;IMG alt="Red Flag Building" src="http://bmetz2.home.xs4all.nl/images/command/briefetc/RF17/descrpt1.jpg"&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario puts you in charge of a night Blue package with AI and DT tasking in the second week of&amp;nbsp;exercise Red Flag 17-3, and it is up to you to make it work.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;To give you an idea of the scope, airplanes scheduled to fly today are as follows: &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Blue Air:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Venom Flight – Royal Air Force Typhoons x&amp;nbsp;8 –&amp;nbsp;OCA / AI&amp;nbsp;tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Ascot&amp;nbsp;Flight –&amp;nbsp;Royal Air Force Tornado GR4As&amp;nbsp;x 4 –&amp;nbsp;AI tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Savage&amp;nbsp;Flight –&amp;nbsp;Royal Australian&amp;nbsp;Air Force F/A-18Fs x 4 – AI tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Victory Flight –&amp;nbsp;US Navy&amp;nbsp;F/A-18Fs x 8 –&amp;nbsp;OCA / SEAD&amp;nbsp;tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Phoenix / Scorp Flights –&amp;nbsp;US Navy EA-18Gs x 6 – SEAD tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Combat&amp;nbsp;Flight –&amp;nbsp;US Marine Corps&amp;nbsp;F-35Bs x&amp;nbsp;6 – AI tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Pulsar&amp;nbsp;Flight – US Air Force F-22s x&amp;nbsp;10 –&amp;nbsp;OCA tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Tiger&amp;nbsp;Flight – US Air Force&amp;nbsp; F-15Es x&amp;nbsp;10 –&amp;nbsp;AI tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Vegas&amp;nbsp;Flight – US Air Force&amp;nbsp; F-35As x 4 –&amp;nbsp;AI tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Gambler Flight – US Air Force F-16CJs x 12 – SEAD / AI tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Chosen Flight – US Air Force F-15Cs x 8 – OCA tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Hoosier Flight&amp;nbsp;– US Air&amp;nbsp;National Guard F-16Cs x 4 –&amp;nbsp;SEAD tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Dragon Flight&amp;nbsp;–&amp;nbsp;Royal Australian&amp;nbsp;Air Force KC-30A x 1 – AAR tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Baja / Enco / Mobil Flights – US Air Force KC-135s x 3 – AAR tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Darth Flight – US Air Force B-2As x 2 – AI tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Gremlin Flight – US Air Force B-52Hs x 2 – SEAD/AI tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;King Flight – US Air Force HC-130J x&amp;nbsp;1 –&amp;nbsp;CSAR tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Jolly Flight –&amp;nbsp;US Air Force MH-60Gs x&amp;nbsp;2 –&amp;nbsp;CSAR tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Stalker Flight - US Army MH-47Gs x 2 –&amp;nbsp;CSAR tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Sandy Flight - US Air Force A-10C x 2 –&amp;nbsp;CSAR support&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Faker Flight – US Air Force EC-130H x 1 – SEAD tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Nightstar Flight – US Air Force E-8C x 1 – Battle Management tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Chalice&amp;nbsp;Flight – US Air Force E-3G x 1 – AEW / Battle Management tasking&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Deepsea&amp;nbsp;Flight –&amp;nbsp;US Navy&amp;nbsp;EP-3E x&amp;nbsp;1 –&amp;nbsp;ISR tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Vulcan Flight –&amp;nbsp;Royal Air Force RC-135W x&amp;nbsp;1 –&amp;nbsp;ISR tasking &lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Logic Flight – US Air Force MC-12W x 1 – ISR&amp;nbsp;tasking&amp;nbsp;&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Reaper Flight – US Air Force MQ-9Bs x&amp;nbsp;3 – ISR&amp;nbsp;tasking&amp;nbsp;(out of Creech AFB)&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Beast Flight – US Air Force RQ-170As x&amp;nbsp;2 – ISR&amp;nbsp;tasking&amp;nbsp;(out of Creech AFB)&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Hawk Flight – US Air Force RQ-4Bs x&amp;nbsp;2 – ISR&amp;nbsp;tasking&amp;nbsp;(out of Creech AFB)&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;IMG alt="Vipers in Vegas" src="http://bmetz2.home.xs4all.nl/images/command/briefetc/RF17/descrpt2.jpg"&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Red Air is flying a large&amp;nbsp;number of F-15s and F-16s out of Nellis as your adversary. They will replicate certain threat types, which will be discussed in more detail in the Blue brief. Red Air will be able to regenerate several times in order to provide proper opposition. You will not have to worry about managing that part though, MiG-1 has it under control :)&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Scenario Designer's notes&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;BR&gt;I hope you enjoy this scenario. Some advice to give you the optimum experience: &lt;BR&gt;- You can load six included custom overlays to make the playing area and in particular your target areas come alive a bit more. I recommend you put the files in the folder Command Modern Air Naval Operations\Overlay\Red Flag 2017\ and load them from there. The filenames start with numbers and they &lt;B&gt;should be loaded in order&lt;/B&gt;. This is because the more detailed target areas need to be on top of the less detailed larger area ones. So 1-flot.png, 2-vegasoverview.png, 3-targetoverview.png, 4-nellis.png, 5-northtarget.png and 6-southtarget.png &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;- If you use the overlays it is recommended that you have the Relief layer &lt;U&gt;dis&lt;/U&gt;abled and BMNG &lt;U&gt;en&lt;/U&gt;abled (the scenario should start up this way, feel free to check in the "View" menu).&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;- Additionally I recommend that you turn off the "Scenario Events" notifications in the Game Options -&amp;gt; Message log menu. Otherwise you will see when certain events are fired and it will give you unrealistic SA about who is scrambling etc. &lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;- However, be sure to turn &lt;B&gt;on&lt;/B&gt; "Special Messages" as this will help with any DT tasking. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;- Be sure to check all the side doctrine settings so that they are to your liking (for example, I play with Automatic Evasion set to "No" so that is how this scenario starts. Check for yourself!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;- I do&amp;nbsp;recommend you&amp;nbsp;leave off "RTB when Winchester" doctrine and also do not just order units to RTB in the middle of the fighting area but guide them most of the way home first. Otherwise they may get themselves stuck on the&amp;nbsp;inaccessible&amp;nbsp;airspace.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Of course feel free to do as you wish (for example you do not &lt;STRONG&gt;have&lt;/STRONG&gt; to use all available assets if you don't want to).&amp;nbsp;Have fun and please let me know what you think in the &lt;A href="http://www.matrixgames.com/forums/tt.asp?forumid=1154" target=_BLANK&gt;Matrixgames Command forums&lt;/A&gt; where you can find me under the name Tomcat84. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Note that this is NOT an easy or simple scenario. Just setting up a couple of AI generated strike missions will most likely not be a success. This scenario requires some thought out planning and a lot of micro managing if you want to be truly succesful. Hence this is &lt;STRONG&gt;not recommended for beginners&lt;/STRONG&gt; or for those who like a quick walk in the park.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Also, an internet connection is useful in order to get all the images in the briefing. (and the atmospheric ones like&amp;nbsp;this one&amp;nbsp;:) ) &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;IMG alt="F-15E on the Nellis ramp" src="http://bmetz2.home.xs4all.nl/images/command/briefetc/RF17/descrpt3.jpg"&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
